# Line endings are the repository's decision, not the machine's.
#
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its system config, so a clone on
# Windows checked every file out with CRLF while a clone on macOS or Linux got
# LF -- and this working tree had drifted into holding both at once. The
# repository itself has always stored LF; this makes the working tree match it
# everywhere, whatever any individual has in their global config.
#
# `text=auto` still lets git detect and leave binaries alone, so images or
# fonts added later need no rule here.
* text=auto eol=lf
